  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans \r\n\r\nLocation Plan, HA-1069-100-PP-LGF Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Lower Ground Floor Plan, HA-1069-101-PP-GF Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Ground Floor Plan, HA-1069-102-PP-RG Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Rear Garden Plan, HA-1069-103-PP-1F Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed First Floor Plan, HA-1069-104-PP-2F Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Second Floor Plan, HA-1069-105-PP-3F Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Third Floor Plan, HA-1069-105-PP-RF Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Roof Plan, HA-1069-110-PE-FR Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Front Elevation, HA-1069-111-PE-RE Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Rear Elevation, HA-1069-112-EE-SI Rev P3 - Existing Side Elevation, HA-1069-113-PE-SI Rev P3 - Proposed Side Elevation, HA-1069-120-ES-AA Rev P3 - Existing Section AA, HA-1069-121-PS-AA Rev P3 - Proposed Section AA, HA-1069-122-PS-BB Rev P3 - Existing & Proposed Section BB, HA-1069-130-PE-SH Rev P3 - Proposed Front & Side Elevation, HA-1069-000-SP Rev P1 - Site Plan\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - The outbuilding hereby approved shall only be used for purposes incidental to the use of the main property (31 Gondar Gardens) and shall not be used as a separate residential dwelling or a business premises.   \r\nReason: To safeguard the amenity of the residential use, adjoining premises, and the area generally in accordance with policies A1 and A4 of the Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the commencement of works on site, tree protection measures shall be installed and working practices adopted in accordance with the document entitled \"Tree Survey, Arboricultural Impact Assessment, Arboricultural Method Statement and Tree Protection Plan\" dated 27/03/2026 by Usherwood Arboriculture ref. BS 5837:2012.  All trees on the site, or parts of trees grow from adjoining sites, unless shown on the permitted drawings as being removed, shall be retained and protected from damage in accordance with BS5837:2012 and with the approved protection details. The development shall be monitored by the project arboriculturalist in accordance with the approved report.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the development will not have an adverse effect on existing trees and in order to maintain the character and amenity of the area in accordance with the requirements of policies A2 and A3 of the Camden Local Plan.\r\n"
  ],
